# width: 120
# height: 40
# The methodology trap behind the 2026-09-21 hunt: headless, `Shift+F10`
# straight after `view.focus_tree` toasted `no tree row under the
# cursor`, while the same two keys in the live app opened the menu — so
# a hunter reading only the headless screen would file a bug that is not
# there, and one reading only the live app would never see this one.
#
# It is a real ordering bug, not the harness. The tree's row list is
# built by its own painter (`Tree.draw` scans once and latches
# `loaded`), and in a `.test` the app starts before the script's `write`
# steps land — so the one scan finds an empty workspace and nothing ever
# re-scans. Every command that READS `app.tree.rows` then sees nothing.
# `view.context_menu_at_focus` scans before giving up now, so headless
# and live agree.
#
# `tree_menu_clipboard.test` is the same menu with an explicit `key r`
# first; this file is the one that must work WITHOUT it.
write a.txt "a"
write b.txt "b"
open a.txt

command view.focus_tree
command view.context_menu_at_focus
expect screen contains "Open in split"
expect screen contains "Rename…"
key esc
expect screen lacks "Open in split"

# The cursor row is the one the menu names, with no refresh in between.
key end
command view.context_menu_at_focus
expect screen contains "b.txt"
key esc

# And the scan is a fallback, not a re-scan on every press: a second
# Shift+F10 on the same rows opens the same menu.
command view.context_menu_at_focus
expect screen contains "Open in split"
key esc
